<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  EARLY BASELINE (Gate 1.1). This declares the app's currently provable data
  collection and required-reason API use. It is intentionally conservative
  (over-declaring is safer than under-declaring). The FINAL App Privacy /
  privacy-manifest audit against the Release archive is Gate 3 and remains
  authoritative. All collected data is linked to the user's account; NONE of it
  is used for tracking (no ATT, no cross-app/data-broker sharing).
  Note: precise location is transmitted only to service the real-time
  nearby-tennis-court request and is not retained; it is declared here
  conservatively for App Functionality.
  v1 de-scope (Milestone 2), source-level data audit (2026-09-05):
   - Health REMOVED — not merely because HealthKit is gone, but because a code/backend
     audit found NO specifically-requested structured health/medical field reachable in
     v1: the only structured inputs are TrainingSession (duration, effort_rating, free
     notes) and OnboardingSurvey (skill ratings, skill weaknesses, goals). All
     injury/pain/readiness/HRV/sleep inputs lived in now-disabled DailyReadiness /
     smartwatch / AI Coach. Per Apple's App Privacy guidance, a generic free-form field
     (TrainingSession notes) that a user *might* use for health text is Other User
     Content (already declared), not the Health category.
   - PurchaseHistory REMOVED — no purchasable Premium in v1.
   - Fitness RETAINED — v1 still collects self-entered training/workout/exercise data
     (sessions, drills, saved workouts) sent to and retained by the backend.
  Final authoritative privacy audit against the Release archive remains Gate 3.1.
-->

<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeEmailAddress</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
